{"type":"assistant","uuid":"a5eba7a3-3fdf-44df-a5a0-6c2614992c44","session_id":"a7d6967c-10b2-44d7-b4f1-f8dcd9af9389","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"a5eba7a3-3fdf-44df-a5a0-6c2614992c44","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root cause:** When a file operation (copy, move, delete, rename) completes, `reloadCurrentDirectory()` is called, which calls `loadPath(currentDirectory)`. This creates a **new** `FileArrayAdapter` and sets it on the `ListView` via `setAdapter()`, which resets the scroll position to the top.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nModified `reloadCurrentDirectory()` in `FileActivity.java` to:\n1. **Save** the scroll position before reloading (first visible item index + pixel offset from top)\n2. **Reload** the directory as before\n3. **Restore** the scroll position using `setSelectionFromTop()` with the saved values\n\n## The Patch\n\n```diff\n     public void reloadCurrentDirectory() {\n+        // Save scroll position before reload\n+        int firstVisibleItem = fileListView.getFirstVisiblePosition();\n+        View v = fileListView.getChildAt(0);\n+        int topOffset = (v != null) ? v.getTop() : 0;\n+\n         loadPath(currentDirectory);\n+\n+        // Restore scroll position after reload\n+        fileListView.setSelectionFromTop(firstVisibleItem, topOffset);\n     }\n```\n\n## Verification\n- ✅ Build successful (`./gradlew clean assembleDebug`)\n- ✅ No compilation errors\n- ✅ Uses `setSelectionFromTop()` (not deprecated) which precisely preserves both the item index and pixel offset for a smooth user experience"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33396,"output_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":31440,"total_tokens":33738}}}
